{
  "id": "murphy-shakti8-feelgood-1phase-temporofrontal",
  "name": "8 Coil Shakti Feelgood: one phase, temporo-frontal (user variant)",
  "category": "mood",
  "evidence": "anecdote",
  "fidelity": "approximation",
  "dose": {"value": [10, 50], "unit": "mG", "plane": "unstated", "cite": "Murphy, measurement.htm"},
  "origin": "An 8 Coil Shakti user, reported on Todd Murphy's blog; variant of Murphy's one-phase Feelgood session",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "A user-reported variant of Murphy's one-phase Feelgood session with the four coils moved from the frontal lobes to the temporo-frontal area, where the frontal and temporal lobes meet. It rests on one reader comment under the vendor's blog post (24 August 2017). Same signal: the amygdala and hippocampal signals one after the other with 4-s pauses.",
  "notes": "The source is one reader comment of 24 August 2017 under the vendor's blog post '8 Coil Shakti feelgood session' (sacredneurology.com): 'I decided to try the one phase \"feelgood\" over the temporo-frontal area using the amygdala and hippocampus signals. I really just felt good after a 30 min session.' A 60-min session followed. Sites, polarity and coil count are not in the comment. This program uses F7, FT7, F8 and FT8 on CH5-8, all driven together. Sites and polarity are project choices: F7 and FT8 are reversed. Phase 1 (30 min) is the 30-min version: stop after it, or let phase 2 run for the 60-min version. One pass: amygdala signal, 4 s of silence, hippocampal signal, 4 s of silence. Both are rebuilt: the vendor's files are not published. The amygdala signal is the project's rising sweep (6 to 30 Hz) with the published point duration and length (230 points of 3 ms; Ryczko 2002 p.1 [592]); its point values were never published as numbers. The hippocampal signal is a primed burst on 1-ms points: one pulse, then four pulses 170 ms later, three times in 0.74 s (after Tsang 2004 p.5 [1017]). The vendor says 'the standard signals have 3 msec points' (rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm), so the point duration is this project's choice. The vendor's 10 to 50 mG carries no distance (measurement.htm, duds.htm); an independent meter read 0.1 to 1.0 uT RMS about 9 cm from the coils (Gendle 2012 p.11 [227]). This program's setting is the peak field 20 mm in front of each coil. This placement is one user's report, not a vendor design. Independent sham-controlled tests of God-Helmet-type fields found no field effect (Granqvist 2005, double-blind; Gendle & McGrath 2012, where the experimenter knew the condition). For the 60-min version the vendor's limit applies: 'Do not do more than one hour-long session in three weeks (Excepting two-phase sessions).' (hour.htm). Not a treatment for depression or any illness. Not for people with a psychiatric diagnosis or epilepsy; stop if distressed.",
  "setting": "Not in sensory deprivation: the vendor says the Feelgood session 'should not be done in sensory deprivation', since it is meant for 'outward-looking', 'this-worldly' effects. No time of day is prescribed (the vendor's page on weekly sessions says they 'can be done any time of day'); the vendor notes that the effect often shows only the morning after.",
  "schedule": "Vendor: 6 weekly sessions or 6 sessions every 3 days (never more often than every 72 h), then 3 weeks off. The 60-min version is a one-phase hour-long session, which the vendor allows at most once every three weeks. If a session is interrupted before it ends, wait three days and start it again from the beginning (if you miss a session of an every-3-days series, the vendor says to stop for three weeks).",
  "targets": ["left-temporal-pole", "right-temporal-pole", "lateral-orbitofrontal-cortex"],
  "source": "Murphy, Mood enhancement & the 8 Coil Shakti https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/rotating/shakti_happiness.htm ; Murphy, The Feelgood Session for the 8 Coil Shakti https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/rotating/feelgood_session.htm ; Shakti demo: Feelgood output page https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/output_feelgood.htm ; Shakti demo: Feelgood consent (schedule, coil photos, not in sensory deprivation) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/feelgood_consent.htm ; Shakti demo: Feelgood consent, 2007 version (30-min phases, one channel at a time) https://web.archive.org/web/20071009203302/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/demo/shakti_demo/feelgood_consent.htm ; Murphy, Shakti Software Demo (video; Feelgood channels, single phase of 20 min) https://youtu.be/YhdlkfeXUI8 ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Overcoming dud sessions (50 mG default) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/duds.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Measurement (10 mG normal peak) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/measurement.htm ; Murphy blog: 8 Coil Shakti feelgood session (reports) https://sacredneurology.com/2013/12/23/8-coil-shakti-feelgood-session/ ; Shakti demo: 'Rapid' and 'High-Speed' signals (3-ms points, 4-s latency) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm ; Shakti demo: Formal Discussion (9.6 s of field per minute) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/mono_proposal.htm ; Shakti demo: Random Theta Band output (LTP spectral peak 5.4 Hz) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/5jut4ranconsent.htm ; Baker-Price & Persinger 1996, Percept Mot Skills 83:491 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8902023/ ; Baker-Price & Persinger 2003, Percept Mot Skills 96:965 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12831278/ ; Tsang, Koren & Persinger 2009, Electromagn Biol Med 28:365 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20017627/ ; Ryczko & Persinger 2002, Percept M